Description: XDJ library UI rework (zoom pref, # sort, key traffic light, columns)
 1. New Preferences > Library spinner "Tracks visible in list" (config
    [Library] VisibleRows, default 8, 0 = Off): the library table derives
    row height from the viewport so exactly N rows fit, and scales the
    font to ~45% of the row height (true zoom for small touch displays).
    Off falls back to the stock manual RowHeight/Font settings.
 2. Rekordbox track lists and playlists always open sorted by # (playlist
    position) ascending. Root cause: RekordboxPlaylistModel declared the
    position column as its default sort but the view preferred the saved
    header sort state; a new TrackModel::forceDefaultSort() hook lets the
    model reassert its default on every load.
 3. Pioneer-style key traffic light: the Key cell is highlighted green
    when the track's key is Camelot-compatible (same key, relative
    major/minor, +/-1 step; KeyUtils::getCompatibleKeys) with the master
    deck's track. Master = the currently playing deck that started
    playing most recently; when no deck is playing nothing is
    highlighted. Keys are always displayed as musical note names
    (Traditional notation), never Camelot numbers.
 4. Rekordbox views show a fixed column set in the visual order
    #, Title, Artist, Key, Duration, with proportional widths that fill
    the viewport (# / Key / Duration sized to content, Artist/Title
    sharing the rest 40/60, Duration stretching to the right edge),
    recomputed on every resize.
